{"name":"Baby Blue Eyes","hex":"#a1caf1","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"baby blue eyes","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various flowering plants in the genus Nemophila, with blue flowers, native from Baja California to Oregon.","A rich tone of baby blue."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baby_blue_eyes"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nemophila menziesii","blocks":[{"text":"Nemophila menziesii, known commonly as baby blue eyes or baby's-blue-eyes, is an annual herb, native to western North America."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Nemophila_menziesii_7794.JPG/330px-Nemophila_menziesii_7794.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nemophila_menziesii"},{"title":"Eye color","blocks":[{"text":"Eye color is a polygenic phenotypic trait determined by two factors: the pigmentation of the eye's iris and the frequency-dependence of the scattering of light by the turbid medium in the stroma of the iris."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Farbverlauf_Augenfarben.jpg/330px-Farbverlauf_Augenfarben.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eye_color"},{"title":"Baby blue","blocks":[{"text":"Baby blue, also called light blue, is a tint of azure, which is one of the pastel colors."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baby_blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Nemophila_menziesii_7794.JPG/500px-Nemophila_menziesii_7794.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Nemophila_menziesii_7794.JPG/1280px-Nemophila_menziesii_7794.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Nemophila_menziesii_7794